---

Portions of FGX's userland are derived from 2.11BSD and remain subject to the
copyright of The Regents of the University of California under the original BSD
license. Those files carry an SPDX/FGX-Provenance header retaining the UCB
copyright notice, and every such file is listed in docs/PROVENANCE.md. The
notice-retention requirement of the BSD license is satisfied by those headers;
FGX's own changes are offered under the BSD-2-Clause license above.

---

Third-party components.  Some programs and libraries in this tree are not
under the BSD-2-Clause licence above, and each file says which licence it is
under in its SPDX-License-Identifier header; docs/PROVENANCE.md lists every
one with its upstream:

- frotz (src/userland/frotz): GPL-2.0-or-later.  The Z-machine interpreter,
  a separate program; a binary distribution that ships it must offer its
  source, as the GPL requires.
- novi (src/userland/novi): BSD-2-Clause, Copyright (c) Dave Plummer.  The
  upstream carries no license file; its author stated the terms: "you can
  assume NOVI is under the 2_BSD license".
- The soft double (toolchain/lib/libdouble/softdouble.c): Apache-2.0, from
  the W65816 fork of llvm-mos; the licence text is
  vendor/65816-llvm-mos/LICENSE.TXT (Apache License v2.0 with LLVM
  Exceptions).
- cron and crontab: LicenseRef-Vixie-Cron, Paul Vixie's terms, reproduced in
  each file.
- ntp: LicenseRef-UMD-NTP, the University of Maryland NTP 3.4 sources as
  2.11BSD ships them; their headers state no licence.
- Four files of elvis (src/userland/elvis): LicenseRef-Elvis, Steve
  Kirkendall's terms: "Elvis is freely redistributable, in either source form
  or executable form.  There are no restrictions on how you may use it."
- The console fonts disk_src/lib/fonts/default.fnt and bold.fnt: MIT, as
  each file's header states.
- The time zone code and data under vendor/tzcode-* and vendor/tzdata-*:
  public domain, except date.c, newstrftime.3 and strftime.c, which are
  BSD-3-Clause, as their LICENSE files state.
